AbelianVarieties/TateModule.lean
--------------------------------
Points are now geometric points: morphisms from `gspec K` = Spec K̄ (with
K̄ = `AlgebraicClosure K`), instead of K-points from `specᵤ K`.

[ ] int_hom_rational                                                 (l.34)
      On points, [n] is multiplication by n: n • g = g ≫ [n]_ A.

[ ] rational_torsion                                                 (l.37)
      Every K̄-point of A[n] is killed by n.
      Still missing: the inductive step and the final goal.

[ ] finite_torsion_points                                            (l.54)
      A[n](K̄) is finite when n ≠ 0.
      The old proof (for K-points) is kept in a comment below the sorry.
      It needs adapting to K̄-points: send g to Γ(X, ⊤) →ₐ[K] K̄ instead of
      Γ(X, ⊤) →ₐ[B] B, and use that a finite K-algebra has only finitely
      many K-algebra maps into K̄.

[ ] torsion_map_comp                                                 (l.156)
      The maps A[n](K̄) → A[m](K̄) compose correctly: going n → m → k
      equals going n → k directly (for k ∣ m ∣ n).
      Done: the arithmetic n / k = (m / k) * (n / m).
      Still missing: the scheme-level identity
        ker_int_hom (k ∣ n) = ker_int_hom (m ∣ n) ≫ ker_int_hom (k ∣ m)
      (probably pullback.hom_ext + int_hom_comp).

[ ] tate_module_representation                                       (l.242)
      A homomorphism f : A → B induces T_ p (A) → T_ p (B).
      functorial_ker_int (IntHom.lean) is now done, so this is unblocked.
      Note: f and [IsAddMonHom f] are section variables not mentioned in
      the statement, so they are currently NOT arguments of this def
      (needs `include f in` or explicit binders).
